+### Other sources beyond SLO (second pass)
+
+None of these gives an official per-year table, but together they give anchors for years 1–3. All are search excerpts, not full reads.
+
+| Source | Type | What it says |
+|---|---|---|
+| [Chr. Lyceum Delft, level scheme](https://www.chrlyceumdelft.nl/molenhuispad/Onderwijs/anglia-niveaus) | School page | Onderbouw: havo **A2**, vwo **A2/B1**. Bovenbouw: havo **B1**, vwo **B2**. |
+| [AMN, Engels productinformatie](https://amn.nl/onderwijs/taal-en-rekentoetsen/productinformatie-engels.pdf) | Test provider | Onderbouw targets: havo **A2**, vwo **A2/B1**, vmbo kb/gl/tl **A1/A2** (skill headings not visible). |
+| [Nuffic, "B2 or not B2"](https://www.nuffic.nl/sites/default/files/2020-08/rapport-b2-or-not-b2-taalvaardigheden-en-erk-niveaus-in-tweetalig-onderwijs.pdf) | Bilingual-education (TTO) report | End of onderbouw (year 3) in TTO: vwo-tto **B2**, havo-tto **B1**, all skills. This is a stricter standard than regular classes. |
+| [Cambridge English NL, havo](https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/nl/exams-and-tests/general-english-and-for-schools/havo/), [vwo](https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/nl/exams-and-tests/general-english-and-for-schools/vwo/index.aspx), [vmbo](https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/nl/exams-and-tests/general-english-and-for-schools/vmbo/) | Commercial | Havo starts klas 1 at **A2**; vmbo klas 1 at **A1/A2**; B1 Preliminary suggested for vmbo klas 3–4 and onderbouw havo/vwo; B2 First for havo 5 and vwo 4–5. A teacher source puts vwo 6 at **B2/C1**. |
+| [SLO tussendoelen onderbouw](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/3940/advies-tussendoelen-kernvakken-onderbouw-vo.pdf) | Official advice | Differentiated for 2 vmbo-b, 2 vmbo-k, 2 vmbo-gt, 3 havo and 3 vwo. **Not read** — it is the most promising official source for years 1–3. |
+| [SLO study, end-of-programme speaking](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/3186/eindniveau-gespreksvaardigheid-engels-in-het-voortgezet-onderwijs.pdf) | Official research | 1,722 final-year students; attained: vmbo-bb **A1**, kb **A2**, gt **A2/B1**, havo **B2**. |
+
+Also: the ERK reportedly has no formal status in vmbo, and no national Cito or Inspectie survey of English per school year in secondary education turned up (the Inspectie 2019 *peil.Engels* is about primary school).
+
+**What this suggests about the app's table:** the app's year-3 values (havo B1, vwo B1–B2) match the **bilingual-education** end-of-year-3 standard and the Cambridge B1 Preliminary suggestion, while the regular-class school and test-provider figures are one step lower (A2 and A2/B1). That is a hypothesis, not proof of where the table came from. In any case the table looks like an *approximation* rather than an official figure.
+
+**Candidate replacement table (my interpolation, for teacher review — not data):** official end-of-programme anchors, start anchors from the sources above, and ranges in between.
+
+| Year | VMBO-bb | VMBO-kb | VMBO-tl | HAVO | VWO |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| jaar 1 | A1 | A1–A2 | A1–A2 | A2 | A2 |
